+## 09-29 — MINMAX-1: min/max reductions on x86-64, and the instrument that hid them
+<!-- src: engineering/evidence/MINMAX-1/README.md -->
+
+Two independent defects, both found by measurement, both fixed together.
+
+**The compiler.** `integer min/max` over `int[]` never vectorized on x86-64.
+The reduction only becomes a `Select` after the pass pipeline's `if_convert`
+phase, which runs AFTER the main vectorizer, so a late rerun exists to catch
+it — but that rerun was gated on `matches!(target, Aarch64)` while its own
+comment promised "x86-64 reruns the AVX2 pass". The finished
+`VecMaxI32x8`/`vpmaxsd` + `VecHorizontalMaxI32x8` machinery was therefore
+dead code on x86, and `Min` did not exist at all. Fixed by sharing ONE
+dispatch table between the early and late runs (so the late run cannot drift
+from the early run's ISA/FP configuration) and opening it to x86-64, plus a
+`ReductionKind::Min` mirror (detector, `vpminsd`, new
+`VecHorizontalMinI32x8`) and admission of the IV-indexed-GEP shape at
+`iv_init == 0` (the marching-pointer-only rule rejected the ordinary
+`for (i = 0; ...)` loop, which is the shape real code writes).
+
+Measured (`-O3 -march=x86-64-v3`, steady-state density): `min_i32`/`max_i32`
+**1.5 -> 0.1250 insn/byte** (12x) — scalar -> 8-wide `vpminsd`/`vpmaxsd`,
+level with gcc 16.2 and icx (both 0.1250); clang 23.1's 0.0547 is 4x
+unrolling of the same body and is the one gap left.
+
+**A second defect the same measurement exposed.** With min/max packed, its
+steady state was 10 instructions per 32 bytes against GCC's 4 — six of them
+recomputing `n / 8` with a real `divq` EVERY iteration. The transforms
+divide a dynamic limit by inserting a `UDiv` into the loop HEADER, and
+nothing hoists it afterwards (LICM runs before the vectorizer; the late
+rerun after it). Sums happened to be fine (their limit arithmetic was
+strength-reduced and hoisted), min/max was not. Both transforms now emit the
+division once in the preheader as `LShr` (power-of-two width, exact for the
+unsigned division `UDiv` denotes), with a header fallback when the loop has
+no single preheader: 10 -> 4 instructions per trip.
+
+**The miscompile it produced, and the refusal that fixed it.** The min/max
+pattern models ONE accumulator. A loop carrying a second one (`s += a[i]`
+beside `mx = max(mx, a[i])`, or min AND max) was rewritten with that second
+accumulator unmodelled: `mnmax_kernel` returned `sum == 0` for every n below
+the vector width. The detector now refuses any loop whose header carries a
+second accumulator computed inside the body. That refusal is load-bearing and
+pinned by contract 3 of the gate (unsigned, 16-bit, float, guarded and
+multi-accumulator shapes stay scalar AND stay correct).
+
+**The instrument.** `scripts/hot_loop_metric.py` — the tool the project's own
+policy uses to rank loop kernels — had two defects that both flattered LCCC:
+it called every branch to a textually earlier label a backedge (so a
+composite `matmul` shell was measured, reporting 0.0117 insn/byte for a
+kernel that really costs 0.1172), and its step recovery only recognised a
+pointer advance on a register appearing in a memory operand (so LCCC's
+index-addressed packed loops measured as "step unknown" and the scalar
+remainder was reported instead — a vectorized kernel recorded as scalar).
+Both are fixed with a real CFG: iterative dominators, natural loops, nesting
+classification, `composite` loops carrying NO density, and address-advance
+recovery that follows one level of `movslq`/`lea` scaling. Nine known-answer
+tests (`scripts/test_hot_loop_metric.py`, now a CI gate) plus the captured
+LCCC/GCC 16.2 `matmul` pair in `tests/asm/hot-loop/`.
+
+**Where the ranking now disagrees with the static rank.** `matmul` is ranked
+"63 instructions behind GCC" by `codegen_oracle.py --rank` and 1.60x AHEAD by
+density; `zlib_ng_adler32` is "259 behind" statically and 8.7x ahead by
+density. Static ranking rewards refusing to vectorize, and the corpus is
+mostly loops. [fix][rec][goal]
+
+---
+
+## 09-29 — Review-AI audit of PR #674, and LOOP-PREHEADER-1
+
+Rebased on upstream `800b439f` (PR #674 ZERO-REM-1/SPILL-01 and PR #675
+assembler work both merged). Full response to the five audit findings:
+[`engineering/evidence/LINKGATE-1/`](../evidence/LINKGATE-1/README.md).
+
+**Agreed and fixed (4):** the linker gate's `inapplicable` class had no
+applicability floor (now `min(2, len(oracles))` + the bfd reference must have
+an opinion + `errored` for non-{0,1} exits, classified *before* the `shared`
+shortcut, which the auditor's placement would have missed);
+`check_vec_remainder_shapes.py`'s module docstring contradicted its own
+`count_loops()` (backward branches vs CFG SCCs); the
+`rewire_escaping_iv_uses` comment claimed ZERO-REM-1 reaches the `None` arm,
+which is false — the dead-mirror case passes `Some(trip_val)`; and
+`slot_census.rs` read the process-global target width (now a parameter).
+
+**Disagreed (1, F5 in part):** the census's global read was not a
+cross-compilation defect specific to that file — `regalloc.rs` reads the same
+global at four sites, so de-globalising one caller buys nothing and a future
+i686 call site passing a wrong constant would be *worse*. Fixed as a
+parameter anyway (explicit + testable) but with a `debug_assert` against the
+process target, so it cannot drift, and the honest framing recorded.
+
+**The auditor's F4 conclusion was right for the wrong reason.** "Do not touch
+the `debug_assert!(false)`" holds, but not because the `None` arm is
+unreachable by ZERO-REM-1: it is reachable via the AVX2/SSE2 reduction paths
+whenever `insert_reduction_remainder_loop` declines. What makes it
+unreachable is the DOMINANCE PRECONDITION (`reduction_remainder_references_sound`)
+checked before any IR is touched. The rewritten comment records that chain and
+warns against *both* relaxing the assert and "fixing" it into a conditional.
+
+**LOOP-PREHEADER-1** (new, `src/passes/loop_preheader.rs`): LICM refuses to
+hoist a derived-pointer load unless the loop's preheader is dedicated — a
+correct gate, but LCCC never *created* a dedicated preheader, so the gate
+refused essentially every invariant parameter load in the corpus. The pass
+splices an empty block onto the outside edge. First measurement: **ungated it
+was +7 instructions** (27 insertions that unlocked nothing, because the
+guard-at-top header holds no loads and LICM's must-execute rule refused them
+all). Shipped **profitability-gated**: 0 insertions and byte-identical output
+by default. With `CCC_LOOP_ROTATE=1` it fires 18 times and cuts the
+`fir_filter` FIR hot loop **56 → 38 instructions (−32 %)**. Rotation stays
+off: it is +2.6 % corpus-wide because `loop_rotate` materialises the loop
+condition as an `i1` (`setl; movzbl; testb; jne` where one `jl` belongs) —
+recorded as LOOP-PREHEADER-2 and deliberately not bundled.
+
+**`loop_rotate` is also outright broken on 2 corpus programs.** Under
+`CCC_VALIDATE_SSA=1` with rotation forced on, `fir_filter.c` and
+`moving_stats.c` abort with `SSA PHI-ARITY VIOLATION after phase 'after iter=0
+loop_rotate'`: phi incoming-label sets that do not match the rewritten CFG.
+Not ours — it reproduces with `CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=loop_preheader`, and it fires at Phase
+2b, before the preheader pass runs at all. That is very likely why rotation is
+opt-in, and it is a concrete target for LOOP-PREHEADER-2. [neg][rec]
+
